  "task": {
    "objective": "Deliver all six construction crates while building, sharing, anchoring or drifting real pontoon routes across the harbor channel.",
    "natural_termination": "Success when all six crates are delivered. Failure when a worker lacks physical support after tide/current update or any crate sinks. Failure excludes success on the same step.",
    "interaction": "One anchor stabilizes a whole lashed component; releasing it can carry a peer and their cargo to a different row. Sharing, unsharing, lifting and lashing sections change peer movement permissions and connectivity, with a permanent detour and a low-tide causeway as alternatives.",
